 ## Overview
-Fine-tuning in 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) refers to the phase where a pre-initialized set of Gaussian primitives—often generated via a feed-forward network or sparse initialization—is optimized to achieve photorealistic novel view synthesis [S1]. It solves the problem of initializing high-fidelity radiance fields efficiently by leveraging pretrained priors to accelerate convergence and reduce memory consumption compared to training from scratch [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard training by explicitly enabling the growing and pruning of 3D primitives during the optimization process, allowing the model to discard redundant initial Gaussians while refining geometry and color attributes [S1].
+Fine-tuning is the final optimization stage in the 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) training pipeline, designed to refine the geometry, color, and opacity attributes of a pre-initialized set of Gaussian primitives [S1]. It solves the problem of initializing a high-fidelity scene representation by leveraging pretrained priors or feed-forward estimates to accelerate convergence and reduce memory consumption compared to training from scratch [S1]. It sets itself apart from earlier stages by enabling active growing and pruning of primitives to eliminate redundancy inherent in initial estimates, a capability not typically utilized during the initial densification phase [S1].
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Inputs:** A set of initial 3D Gaussian primitives $\{G_i\}$ with predicted geometry (mean $\mu_i$, covariance $\Sigma_i$ or scale/rotation) and color attributes (SH coefficients), typically generated by a feed-forward process [S1]. Input images and camera poses for the target scene.
-*   **Outputs:** Optimized 3D Gaussian primitives with refined geometry and color attributes [S1].
+*   **Input:** A set of initialized 3D Gaussian primitives $\{G_i\}$, where each primitive $i$ has geometry (mean $\mu_i$, covariance $\Sigma_i$ or scale/rotation) and color attributes (SH coefficients $c_i$), typically generated via a feed-forward process or SfM [S1].
+*   **Output:** Optimized Gaussian primitives with refined attributes that achieve photorealistic novel view synthesis [S1].
 
